<title>BELGIUM: Belgian debt/GDP ratio 127 pct in 1997 - govt.</title>
<headline>Belgian debt/GDP ratio 127 pct in 1997 - govt.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said on Tuesday the ratio of the country's debt to gross domestic product would fall to 127 percent in 1997, enabling Belgium to join Europe's single currency.</p>
<p>The debt/GDP ratio had been still at 137 percent in 1993, said the policy statement on the 1997 budget which was being presented to parliament.  </p>
<p>&quot;Thus Belgium will comply in 1997 with all the conditions to be among the first group of countries to be selected at the beginning of 1998 to join economic and monetary union and prepare the conversion of their respective currencies into a single currency, the euro,&quot; the statement said.</p>
